      "text": [
        {
          "id": "title",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "#1 · \"Free for All\" (paraphrased); the ITVX listing order as declared extent",
          "title": "A whole world for obtaining one answer",
          "italic": "The Village embodies the counterfeit gathering: a population assembled for voting and ceremony while the routes by which answers can matter stay controlled (C25).",
          "body": "",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.05,
          "width": 560,
          "size": 30,
          "align": "left"
        },
        {
          "id": "body1",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "The Village can stage the circumstances in which Six acts: an apparent ally part of an interrogation, an escape route returning its user, an invitation bringing resistance inside an administered procedure. \"Free for All\" gives participation electoral form: Six accepts the contest for Number Two after the prospect of meeting Number One is held out; publicity bearing his face is already printed; a reporter supplies answers when he declines.",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 620,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left",
          "w": 520
        },
        {
          "id": "body2",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "He promises freedom, undergoes drugging, wins the vote — and at the Green Dome his attempt to use the office meets violence. Fifty-Eight, previously speaking a language he cannot understand, now addresses him in English and takes authority as incoming Number Two. The election carries Six into the office without giving his command power to end captivity. The intervening episodes remain a declared extent — premises located, not invented.",
          "x": 0.6,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 505,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left"
        }
      ],
