      "text": [
        {
          "id": "title",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "#3 · the political-count carrier; A02 copula; A13; C25; the Syn matheme comparison",
          "title": "The asymmetric count: Two replaces, Six is assigned, One stays withheld",
          "italic": "The scene requires all three numbered offices — and the mytheme is the appointed political counterfeit of the count: the office retains the power of assignment and gives the captive its result.",
          "body": "",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.05,
          "width": 560,
          "size": 30,
          "align": "left"
        },
        {
          "id": "body1",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "The abstraction operates differently at the two ends. Number Two identifies an office through changes of bearer; Number Six identifies a person the office seeks to hold in an assigned position — the office gains continuity across replacement while the captive is denied authority over how his designation counts. Three offices: One the withheld source of command, Two delegated authority, Six the classified answer. A02 defines the difference",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 620,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left",
          "w": 520
        },
        {
          "id": "body2",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "between identifying this participant and making a predicate exhaustive of him; A03 qualifies the demand to close the relation — the institution's concealed information is not the Immutable Gap. The movement from Two to Six compares with the Syn matheme 2+2²=6=4+2, the count including its generating relation: in the Village's speech-act the office keeps assignment's power, giving the captive its result. McGoohan and Markstein are not credited with QL notation.",
          "x": 0.6,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 505,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left"
        }
      ],
